lite-ai-toolkit provides CMake variables (non-target API):

    find_package(lite.ai.toolkit CONFIG REQUIRED)
    include_directories(${lite.ai.toolkit_INCLUDE_DIRS})
    link_directories(${lite.ai.toolkit_LIBS_DIRS})
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE ${lite.ai.toolkit_LIBS})

Note: lite.ai.toolkit unconditionally requires CUDA (nvcc) at build time,
regardless of whether the tensorrt feature is enabled.

To enable TensorRT backend, set the following environment variables before
running vcpkg install, then install with the [tensorrt] feature:

    export CUDA_DIR=/usr/local/cuda-12.9
    export TENSORRT_DIR=/path/to/TensorRT-x.x.x.x
    vcpkg install lite-ai-toolkit[tensorrt]:x64-linux
